BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pl-pit-advance-payment@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=20
SUMMARY:Poland: Employee PIT advance (zaliczka) payment to the tax office (
 monthly)
DESCRIPTION:The employer pays the PIT advance withheld from salaries by the
  20th day of the month following the month in which the salary was paid.\n
 Applies to: Employers withholding PIT on salaries\nNon-working-day rule: c
 heck the source.\n\nSource: https://www.biznes.gov.pl/pl/portal/00234\nDet
 ails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#poland\n\nFor infor
 mation only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule sta
 ted by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last ch
 ecked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#poland
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pl-zus-contributions-legal-entities@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15
SUMMARY:Poland: ZUS contributions and DRA declaration - payers with legal p
 ersonality
DESCRIPTION:The ZUS DRA declaration and monthly reports are submitted and c
 ontributions paid by the 15th day of the following month by payers with le
 gal personality (for example limited companies).\nApplies to: Payers with 
 legal personality (e.g. sp. z o.o.\, S.A.\, foundations)\nNon-working day:
  If the end of the deadline falls on a public holiday\, Saturday or Sunday
 \, the next working day counts as the last day.\nSource for non-working-da
 y rule: https://www.zus.pl/en/firmy/rozliczenia-z-zus/dokumenty-rozliczeni
 owe/termin-skladania-dokumentow-i-oplacania-skladek\n\nSource: https://www
 .zus.pl/en/firmy/rozliczenia-z-zus/dokumenty-rozliczeniowe/termin-skladani
 a-dokumentow-i-oplacania-skladek\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.
 eu/deadlines.html#poland\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice
 . Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holi
 days are not applied. Sources last checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#poland
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pl-zus-contributions-other-payers@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=20
SUMMARY:Poland: ZUS contributions and DRA declaration - other payers
DESCRIPTION:The ZUS DRA declaration and monthly reports are submitted and c
 ontributions paid by the 20th day of the following month by other payers\,
  such as sole traders and partnerships without legal personality that empl
 oy staff.\nApplies to: Payers without legal personality that employ staff 
 (e.g. sole traders\, partnerships)\nNon-working day: If the end of the dea
 dline falls on a public holiday\, Saturday or Sunday\, the next working da
 y counts as the last day.\nSource for non-working-day rule: https://www.zu
 s.pl/en/firmy/rozliczenia-z-zus/dokumenty-rozliczeniowe/termin-skladania-d
 okumentow-i-oplacania-skladek\n\nSource: https://www.zus.pl/en/firmy/rozli
 czenia-z-zus/dokumenty-rozliczeniowe/termin-skladania-dokumentow-i-oplacan
 ia-skladek\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#pola
 nd\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the rec
 urring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. 
 Sources last checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#poland
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pl-pit-11-annual@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270131
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270201
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=1;BYMONTHDAY=-1
SUMMARY:Poland: PIT-11 annual income information to the tax office
DESCRIPTION:PIT-11 and PIT-R are sent to the tax office by the end of Janua
 ry of the year following the tax year (and PIT-11 to the taxpayer by the e
 nd of February).\nApplies to: Employers and other payers of employment inc
 ome\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.podatk
 i.gov.pl/podatki-osobiste/pit/platnik\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpay
 roll.eu/deadlines.html#poland\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax a
 dvice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and
  holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#poland
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pl-pit-4r-annual@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270131
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270201
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=1;BYMONTHDAY=-1
SUMMARY:Poland: PIT-4R annual return of withheld advances
DESCRIPTION:PIT-4R is prepared and sent only to the tax office by the end o
 f January of the year following the tax year.\nApplies to: Employers and o
 ther payers withholding PIT advances\nNon-working-day rule: check the sour
 ce.\n\nSource: https://www.podatki.gov.pl/podatki-osobiste/pit/platnik\nDe
 tails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#poland\n\nFor info
 rmation only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule st
 ated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last c
 hecked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#poland
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
